# SAP Development Rules

## Architecture
- Clean Core only: extensions in customer namespace (Z*, Y*), never modify SAP standard
- Prefer RAP over classic BOPF for new S/4 developments
- S/4HANA patterns; ECC-only only when project is explicitly legacy

## Naming
- CDS views: `ZI_<name>` (interface), `ZC_<name>` (consumption)
- Classes: `ZCL_<name>`, behavior implementations `ZBP_I_<name>`
- Reports: `ZR_<name>`, includes `Z<name>TOP`, `Z<name>F01`

## Code quality
- ABAP 7.57+ syntax where available
- Business logic in classes, not procedural reports
- ABAP Unit tests for validations, calculations, mappings
- No hardcoded credentials, hostnames, or production client IDs

## AI / Cursor usage
- Never paste real customer master data or production dumps
- Use synthetic/mock data in examples
- All generated code requires human review + ADT syntax check before transport
- Document transport order and dependencies in commit/PR message

## Documentation
- Code comments: English (team standard) unless client requires German
- Technical docs / status reports: German or English per client

## Fiori / UI5
- Fiori Elements preferred for RAP OData services
- Freestyle UI5 only when Elements insufficient
- OData V4 for RAP, V2 only for legacy services

## Integrations (CPI/BTP)
- Explicit error handling and retry strategy in mappings
- No secrets in code — use Secure Parameters / Destination Service
